<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!-- THE TRAINING JOBS. Owner's row: "certifications, training jobs".

       Each one is an ordinary bill the player adds to a bench, modelled exactly on
       RR_AssembleMachineGate: a pawn walks over, does the work, and
       RecipeWorker_RimroomsCertification records the qualification against whoever did it. No
       new work giver, no new job driver and no new building.

       NO INGREDIENTS, AND THAT IS CHECKED RATHER THAN ASSUMED. Training costs work and a skill
       floor, not materials - there is nothing physical to consume in a briefing. Eight Core
       recipes ship with no <ingredients> element at all (Sterilize, ButcherCorpseMechanoid and
       six others), read out of the installed game data, so a pure-work recipe is Core practice
       and not a guess.

       CORE ENFORCES THE SKILL FLOOR through skillRequirements, which is the whole reason it is
       declared here rather than checked in code: RimWorld refuses the bill to an unqualified
       pawn up front. A floor tested in Notify_IterationCompleted would mean spending thousands
       of ticks of somebody's day and being told no at the end.

       WHY THE BENCH IS A MACHINING TABLE OR A CRAFTING SPOT, which is a real limitation and is
       recorded rather than hidden. Bills need a Building_WorkTable, and Core ships NO office or
       study worktable - the research benches are Building_ResearchBench and have no bill stack
       at all, so a recipe placed on one would be a certification nobody could ever earn. The
       nineteen Core worktables were enumerated from the installed data to establish that. So
       training happens at the branch's own bench, where the gate hardware and the manuals are:
       TableMachining is already required by gate start-up step 2, so no branch is ever blocked
       on building something new, and CraftingSpot costs nothing for a branch that has not got
       that far. A profile that adds a study bench is not named here and does not need to be -
       the player simply uses the bench they have. -->

  <RecipeDef>
    <defName>RR_TrainGateOperator</defName>
    <label>train gate operator</label>
    <description>Work through the dialling procedure at the branch's bench: what the reserve is doing, which readings mean stop, and how to hold a ramp without watching it climb. Whoever does the work is recorded as a trained gate operator, and a trained operator takes work off every spin-up afterwards.</description>
    <jobString>training on the gate procedure</jobString>
    <workAmount>5000</workAmount>
    <workSkill>Intellectual</workSkill>
    <requiredGiverWorkType>Crafting</requiredGiverWorkType>
    <skillRequirements>
      <Intellectual>4</Intellectual>
    </skillRequirements>
    <workerClass>RimroomsAsyncIndustries.Personnel.RecipeWorker_RimroomsCertification</workerClass>
    <recipeUsers>
      <li>TableMachining</li>
      <li>CraftingSpot</li>
    </recipeUsers>
  </RecipeDef>

  <RecipeDef>
    <defName>RR_TrainFieldAnalyst</defName>
    <label>train field analyst</label>
    <description>Work through somebody else's finished report and learn to say whether the branch can stand behind it. Whoever does the work is recorded as a trained field analyst, and may sign off an analysis whatever their Intellectual.</description>
    <jobString>training on report review</jobString>
    <workAmount>5500</workAmount>
    <workSkill>Intellectual</workSkill>
    <requiredGiverWorkType>Crafting</requiredGiverWorkType>
    <skillRequirements>
      <Intellectual>3</Intellectual>
    </skillRequirements>
    <workerClass>RimroomsAsyncIndustries.Personnel.RecipeWorker_RimroomsCertification</workerClass>
    <recipeUsers>
      <li>TableMachining</li>
      <li>CraftingSpot</li>
    </recipeUsers>
  </RecipeDef>

  <RecipeDef>
    <defName>RR_TrainReserveTechnician</defName>
    <label>train reserve technician</label>
    <description>Strip and rebuild the parts of a gate that wear first, until reconditioning one stops being guesswork. Whoever does the work is recorded as a trained reserve technician, and reconditions a gate for noticeably less work afterwards.</description>
    <jobString>training on gate servicing</jobString>
    <workAmount>6000</workAmount>
    <workSkill>Crafting</workSkill>
    <requiredGiverWorkType>Crafting</requiredGiverWorkType>
    <skillRequirements>
      <Crafting>5</Crafting>
    </skillRequirements>
    <workerClass>RimroomsAsyncIndustries.Personnel.RecipeWorker_RimroomsCertification</workerClass>
    <recipeUsers>
      <li>TableMachining</li>
    </recipeUsers>
  </RecipeDef>

</Defs>
